WEBVTT

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:08.690
Everyone, the project that you're currently involved in is classified.

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:12.980
However, the Coupling system implemented in the Valiancers

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:16.160
will definitely play a role in our war against Zogilia.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.260
Once the Coupling mechas are
deployed to all of the Alliance army,

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:23.750
you will become the army's core.

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:26.810
Keep this in mind while training.

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:30.760
Allow me to introduce the team members.

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:34.510
First, our advocate theorist, Doctor Fermi—

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:40.110
Hey! Dio Weinberg?

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:40.930
Yeah.

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:45.400
I'm Fromm. Looks like we're the youngest pilots in the team.

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:46.690
Nice to meet you, Dio.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:49.440
Nice to meet you.

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:54.840
So you came here from the front line to volunteer.

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:56.110
Any particular reason?

00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:03.620
Fiona...<i></i>

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:04.750
Huh?

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:07.930
I just

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:10.560
want the power to defeat the enemy.

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:12.120
Dio...

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:13.710
Where were you deployed?

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:15.470
Oomura Base.

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:19.470
Oomura? The one that just got bombed?

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:28.900
Spread your wings

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:33.530
See the light of hope in the sky you have yet to witness

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:36.820
And don't ever give in to the weight of sorrow

00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:42.200
Echo unto eternity, "Unisonia"

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:51.460
That world you see before your eyes

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:57.050
I wonder what colors it is made of

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:01.510
The pain of loss isn't something

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:04.470
You want to get used to, and yet

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:09.440
Even on a night like this, the stars glisten

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:16.400
Like a tarnished coin spilling from the palm of your hand

00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:18.240
Can't go back

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:19.660
Want to go home

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:22.990
The two of them back-to-back

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:25.040
Break through

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:29.790
Turning unfading emotions into a lasting bond

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:33.130
Like painting over a colorless world

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:35.840
Let this sympathy reach

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:42.090
Let's build the future that we envision

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:45.310
You'll see, we'll even change fate

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:50.100
Transcending time, "Unisonia"

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:56.820
Zogilia is also broadcasting a video?

00:02:56.820 --> 00:03:01.030
Coincidentally, the enemy is also trying to use propaganda.

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:03.320
The music is quite gallant.

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:06.700
With this, the enemy will be giving their all.

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:08.450
Prepare for battle!

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:09.580
Understood!

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:14.840
It's all because you pulled out a gun, you know?

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:16.750
How would you suggest killing them, then?

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:19.600
I told you, that's not the point.

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:24.890
They're here.

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:26.220
That's...

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:28.930
Our new ship.

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:37.900
The national army's new airship departed from Chitose?

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:39.190
At first glance,

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:44.030
it appears as though they are heading for the Alliance's Hawaii Base to prevent them from regrouping.

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:46.030
Their projected course will lead them right into our battlefield.

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:47.990
It's too late.

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:49.660
By the time they arrive,

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:52.670
the enemy's new-type will be bits and scraps on the seafloor...

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:55.880
The enemy's signal has disappeared.

00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:56.710
What was that?

00:03:56.710 --> 00:04:01.510
When the seas get rough, it's hard to track them.

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:05.550
There's no way an airship that size could get swallowed by rough seas.

00:04:05.550 --> 00:04:06.760
Hurry up and find it!

00:04:07.770 --> 00:04:09.310
Multiple objects detected.

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:10.810
They're islands!

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:15.810
Enemy detected.

00:04:15.810 --> 00:04:17.310
An Imperial Guard airship.

00:04:17.310 --> 00:04:18.360
It's the Gae Bolg!

00:04:18.930 --> 00:04:21.110
This is going to be tough.

00:04:21.110 --> 00:04:23.820
The enemy ship has changed its search pattern.

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:25.820
They've probably lost track of our location.

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:27.740
To reach the Alliance's Hawaii Base,

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:30.290
it'll only take two hours at maximum speed.

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:34.210
They said they can't even afford to send a single ship to help.

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:36.420
We'll have to take care of this ourselves.

00:04:36.820 --> 00:04:39.750
We've got some new equipment on our side.

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:43.630
With regards to electronic warfare,
we'll certainly have a chance against the Gae Bolg.

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:46.680
Perfection isn't necessary.

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:48.800
Time is on our side.

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:53.680
A storm, you say?

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:56.520
Currently, winds are reaching up to speeds of 60 m/s.

00:04:56.520 --> 00:04:58.190
At this rate,

00:04:58.190 --> 00:05:00.650
it'll reach the area in one hour.

00:05:00.650 --> 00:05:03.590
Are you telling me that the Gae Bolg
will be downed by a mere storm?

00:05:03.590 --> 00:05:04.480
No.

00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:09.120
But it'll be impossible for Valiancers to fight with this wind speed.

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:11.740
The enemy may also be planning to pass through here.

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:16.000
Hurry up and find the enemy ship!

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:19.880
The enemy ship is activating electronic sensors.

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:21.050
Electronic jammers!

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:22.300
Activating jammers!

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:30.600
To think that our plan is to simply run past them.

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:32.180
Despite his looks,

00:05:32.180 --> 00:05:36.600
our captain hasn't been shot down once,
and he's been on six ships since his training ship.

00:05:36.970 --> 00:05:39.480
Why don't we attack them first?

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:44.360
They might send out more Valiancers than before, you know.

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:47.910
And compared to them, we've only got four mechas.

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:50.120
Make that five.

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:51.870
Lee-san.

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:52.990
Lieutenant.

00:05:52.990 --> 00:05:53.990
Lee!

00:05:53.990 --> 00:05:56.960
You've already recovered from all those injuries?

00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:00.830
It should only take about three days to fully recover from minor injuries like that,

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:02.750
boy from the past.

00:06:02.750 --> 00:06:04.170
Amazing.

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:06.720
Except you've not <i>completely</i> recovered, you've <i>mostly</i> recovered.

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:10.430
When the doctor says it's alright,
it's the same thing as a complete recovery.

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:12.470
Lieutenant.

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:17.820
I'm Ensign Fromm Vantarhei and have
been deployed to the Cygnus as of today.

00:06:17.820 --> 00:06:20.190
I'm sorry for the late introduction.

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:22.480
Yeah. I've heard about you.

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:24.780
I'm Lee Conrad. Nice to meet you.

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:26.030
Lee.

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:28.560
Ah, sorry.

00:06:29.380 --> 00:06:30.240
Fromm,

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:31.740
Aoba and Dio.

00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:34.080
Elvira has something to say to you guys.

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:35.370
To us?

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:43.710
We'll reach the storm in 40 minutes.

00:06:44.090 --> 00:06:45.460
Prepare the Front Terminal!

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:46.670
Your Excellency!

00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:49.680
We'd be giving away our position!

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:53.640
The Gae Bolg will not be defeated by that feeble white swan!

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:55.180
Activate Front Terminal.

00:06:57.390 --> 00:06:58.890
Front Terminal approaching!

00:06:58.890 --> 00:07:01.440
They're not worried about themselves.

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:02.770
Neutralize the waveform, now.

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:04.310
Neutralizing waveform.

00:07:05.380 --> 00:07:06.730
Neutralization complete.

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:14.240
This is the standard Emphater waveform of a Coupling pilot.

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:15.530
What is this?

00:07:15.530 --> 00:07:16.700
You're talking about brainwaves?

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:19.870
The waveform required for Coupling.

00:07:20.310 --> 00:07:23.380
Previously, the Coupling system had several flaws

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:25.840
and as you know, many sacrifices were made.

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:26.920
Yes.

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:32.590
In order to avoid making the same mistake twice, our team implemented two major changes.

00:07:33.390 --> 00:07:40.100
The first was to minimize delays and signal integration by developing a new cockpit.

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:41.640
A new cockpit?

00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:44.560
Yes. Elvira-san developed it, you know?

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:45.480
Oh.

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:46.610
Is that so?

00:07:46.610 --> 00:07:51.200
And the second was to gather those who have the potential qualities for Coupler Training.

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:59.660
Every Coupler received strict training to match their own Emphater waveform with the standard waveform

00:07:59.660 --> 00:08:02.910
and make them nearly identical to each other.

00:08:02.910 --> 00:08:05.710
Due to those changes, the tests were successful this time.

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:07.420
Incredible.

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:10.380
You were the biggest miscalculation, Aoba-kun.

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:10.920
What?

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:12.550
Look at this next one.

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:15.010
You suddenly appeared,

00:08:15.010 --> 00:08:19.520
matched with our trained couplers, and executed a perfect Coupling.

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:21.270
This is your waveform.

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:28.770
Aoba-kun, your waveform and the
standard waveform are exactly the same.

00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:32.240
If that's a coincidence,
then the probability is astronomical.

00:08:32.710 --> 00:08:34.360
Now here's the problem.

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:36.320
Here's Dio's latest waveform.

00:08:38.630 --> 00:08:39.740
It's off?

00:08:40.010 --> 00:08:41.410
Why?

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:46.460
During the dozens of tests with Marcus, yours were almost always at standard.

00:08:46.460 --> 00:08:51.170
After a few Couplings with Aoba-kun,
your waveform changed.

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:55.680
That's why he couldn't match with me.

00:08:55.680 --> 00:08:57.800
You talk about it like it's not your problem.

00:08:57.800 --> 00:08:58.390
Don't tell me...

00:08:58.390 --> 00:09:03.020
Here's your waveform after
Coupling with Aoba-kun only once.

00:09:04.510 --> 00:09:05.980
Me too?

00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:08.230
But with Aoba,

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:09.360
it's possible.

00:09:10.690 --> 00:09:12.280
It's true.

00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:17.780
On top of that, both of your Emphater levels increased when synchronized.

00:09:18.170 --> 00:09:19.740
What does all this mean?

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:21.910
I still don't understand all of the details.

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:25.460
However, the Coupling was successful,
even with an distorted waveform,

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:28.960
because Aoba-kun maintained the
standard waveform without any training.

00:09:29.230 --> 00:09:31.710
This allowed his Buddy to have a wider margin of deviation.

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:32.630
Margin?

00:09:32.630 --> 00:09:35.510
It means that even if a pilot's waveform
deviates from the standard one,

00:09:35.510 --> 00:09:37.720
you can still do a Coupling.

00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:40.360
Not to mention with trained Couplers.

00:09:40.850 --> 00:09:44.850
Because of that, it causes the Buddy's waveform to deviate.

00:09:45.310 --> 00:09:46.520
What does that mean?

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:48.060
Is that a problem?

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:54.780
Normally, a Buddy with a waveform far from the standard can't perform a Coupling.

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:56.320
Which means that if this continues,

00:09:56.660 --> 00:10:01.830
Dio and Fromm-san will only be able to do Coupling with Aoba-san.

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:06.040
The final goal of the Coupling project was that

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:10.250
a trained Coupler could team up freely with another Buddy to perform a Coupling,

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:12.540
then fight at each battlefield.

00:10:13.010 --> 00:10:17.050
You guys have undergone rigorous
training with that goal in mind.

00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:19.930
Coupling with Aoba-kun is a double-edged sword.

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:23.310
As far as restoring a distorted waveform back to the standard,

00:10:23.310 --> 00:10:30.560
we're still unsure how much time may be needed, or if it's even possible with retraining.

00:10:30.560 --> 00:10:34.690
As I thought, Dio and I can't do Coupling anymore, can we?

00:10:35.060 --> 00:10:37.440
It's possible to try once more.

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:38.450
Then…

00:10:40.260 --> 00:10:41.700
They found us.

00:10:41.700 --> 00:10:43.700
The enemy has discovered us!

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:45.740
We couldn't slip past them.

00:10:45.740 --> 00:10:47.370
It's a symbol of a new unit.

00:10:47.710 --> 00:10:49.120
It's not the Gae Bolg.

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:52.130
What the hell is that?

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:54.590
There's no previous data on it.

00:10:54.590 --> 00:10:56.630
It's a new type of Zogilian ship!

00:10:58.090 --> 00:11:00.220
The enemy ship, the white swan, is at our 12 o'clock.

00:11:00.220 --> 00:11:02.840
As expected of the new-type airship.

00:11:02.840 --> 00:11:03.970
It's my honor, sir.

00:11:04.380 --> 00:11:06.970
Valiancer units ready for launch.

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:08.390
Lieutenant Colonel.

00:11:08.810 --> 00:11:11.100
Relay this information to Lord Dolzief.

00:11:11.830 --> 00:11:12.650
Lieutenant Colonel!

00:11:16.400 --> 00:11:21.070
Will the Imperial Army accept this from the National Army?

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:25.660
If it's from a trustworthy figure, then of course.

00:11:27.010 --> 00:11:30.080
Or are you defying my orders?

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:35.420
Surely you're joking, Secret Services Agent.

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:38.630
Captain, send the white swan's position to the Gae Bolg.

00:11:38.630 --> 00:11:42.180
And if needed, we'll provide support.

00:11:42.180 --> 00:11:43.640
Roger.

00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:45.890
Hina, don't be discouraged.

00:11:45.890 --> 00:11:48.210
There is still a chance for you to clear your name.

00:11:52.890 --> 00:11:55.810
The National Army can be useful sometimes.

00:11:56.250 --> 00:12:00.070
Lieutenant Colonel Alfried said if there's a need for backup, just inform him.

00:12:00.070 --> 00:12:01.360
No need.

00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:04.440
Tell him to sit back and watch.

00:12:04.440 --> 00:12:06.070
Gae Bolg, full speed ahead!

00:12:06.070 --> 00:12:09.330
Full speed ahead. Target is the enemy's new-type ship.

00:12:26.680 --> 00:12:29.180
The enemy new-type isn't approaching us.

00:12:29.580 --> 00:12:31.680
Only the Gae Bolg is approaching us?

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:35.980
Zogilia's National Army and Imperial Army have different chains of command.

00:12:36.590 --> 00:12:40.230
As long as they don't attack at the
same time, we'll still have a chance.

00:12:40.850 --> 00:12:41.940
Battlestations!

00:12:41.940 --> 00:12:44.450
Valiancer units, prepare for launch!

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:48.700
We have to decide now.

00:12:48.700 --> 00:12:49.990
This battle...

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:50.910
No...

00:12:50.910 --> 00:12:51.700
From now on…

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:54.620
Who will Buddy with whom?

00:12:54.620 --> 00:12:56.120
I understand.

00:12:56.120 --> 00:12:59.800
Well then, let's do this in one, two, three.

00:13:03.260 --> 00:13:04.630
Okay.

00:13:09.010 --> 00:13:09.760
One,

00:13:10.100 --> 00:13:10.850
two,

00:13:11.100 --> 00:13:11.720
three!

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:16.140
It's settled then.

00:13:16.140 --> 00:13:16.810
The two of you are Buddies.

00:13:16.810 --> 00:13:17.650
Dio?

00:13:19.820 --> 00:13:22.690
I don't want to waste all my training.

00:13:22.690 --> 00:13:24.240
You understand, Dio?

00:13:25.150 --> 00:13:26.200
Sort of.

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:29.490
Dio!

00:13:30.830 --> 00:13:32.160
Are you really okay with this?

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:36.620
It's true that I'd regret it if my training went to waste.

00:13:36.620 --> 00:13:42.050
But we can't risk testing a Coupling
with Fromm in the midst of battle.

00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:43.460
Dio.

00:13:45.890 --> 00:13:49.390
We don't know if it would return after retraining.

00:13:49.390 --> 00:13:53.680
Besides, putting you in a Beryl by yourself wouldn't help much.

00:13:54.220 --> 00:13:56.100
Let's go. We're running out of time.

00:13:56.100 --> 00:13:58.560
H-Hey! Wait up, Dio.

00:13:58.560 --> 00:13:59.650
What does that mean?!

00:13:59.650 --> 00:14:01.020
It's as I said.

00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:07.070
The storm is coming, be careful!

00:14:07.070 --> 00:14:07.780
Roger!

00:14:09.360 --> 00:14:11.910
Please re-write the CMS for me.

00:14:11.910 --> 00:14:13.340
It's already done.

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:16.000
I just had a feeling things would turn out this way.

00:14:16.490 --> 00:14:17.710
I see.

00:14:17.710 --> 00:14:18.960
What are you talking about?

00:14:18.960 --> 00:14:20.190
Nothing.

00:14:20.790 --> 00:14:22.880
Bradyon launch preparations complete.

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:25.590
What's with him? Luxon, complete.

00:14:29.650 --> 00:14:31.850
Two of the enemy's new-type mecha have launched.

00:14:31.850 --> 00:14:33.850
Okay. Proceed as planned.

00:14:33.850 --> 00:14:34.760
Yes, sir!

00:14:35.660 --> 00:14:37.100
Alfried Gallant,

00:14:37.640 --> 00:14:40.150
watch my victory from the sidelines.

00:14:40.150 --> 00:14:42.730
Enemy's Valiancer units have split into two groups.

00:14:43.230 --> 00:14:44.360
How many units in each?

00:14:44.360 --> 00:14:45.820
Five units in each team.

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:46.900
One team is advancing here.

00:14:47.410 --> 00:14:49.240
We must split up as well.

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:52.370
Valiancer units, send one unit to defend the Cygnus.

00:14:52.710 --> 00:14:56.620
If they're targeting the Coupling mechas, then the
one advancing to the Cygnus should be the diversion.

00:14:57.040 --> 00:14:59.660
Inversely, Luxon and Bradyon will take care of that one.

00:14:59.660 --> 00:15:00.640
Understood!

00:15:01.420 --> 00:15:03.420
We'll stop the rest.

00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:04.420
Understood.

00:15:04.420 --> 00:15:06.130
That's more than enough, Lee!

00:15:06.130 --> 00:15:07.380
No complaints!

00:15:09.380 --> 00:15:11.300
The white thing is not around...

00:15:11.300 --> 00:15:13.300
Wait, their movements don't look right.

00:15:14.720 --> 00:15:16.470
Are they trying to take us on?

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:17.930
We were tricked?

00:15:17.930 --> 00:15:18.560
Don't tell me...

00:15:19.510 --> 00:15:21.190
They're attacking from both sides?

00:15:22.500 --> 00:15:27.940
The battle can be controlled in any way if you have enough reserve forces!

00:15:28.340 --> 00:15:29.150
Shit.

00:15:29.150 --> 00:15:30.030
Get them!

00:15:32.520 --> 00:15:35.660
Luxon and Bradyon are surrounded by ten enemy units!

00:15:35.660 --> 00:15:37.580
The difference in forces is too much.

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:41.620
Damn it! They're sending reinforcements over there!

00:15:41.620 --> 00:15:43.920
They think five mechas is enough for us!

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:45.630
That's a fact!

00:15:46.620 --> 00:15:48.630
What a sizable battle force.

00:15:48.630 --> 00:15:53.510
I'd heard that the Imperial Army ship
had received a majority of the supplies.

00:15:53.880 --> 00:15:56.260
So much to envy.

00:15:56.260 --> 00:15:58.260
If this goes on, it'll end up like last time.

00:15:58.810 --> 00:16:00.770
Don't let yourself get surrounded! Break through!

00:16:00.770 --> 00:16:01.730
Got it!

00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:03.230
Connect with Dio!

00:16:03.620 --> 00:16:04.650
Accept!

00:16:09.050 --> 00:16:10.280
I'll cut my way out!

00:16:11.110 --> 00:16:11.990
Watch out!

00:16:14.610 --> 00:16:15.530
Damn it.

00:16:15.530 --> 00:16:17.700
Have they completely surrounded us already?

00:16:17.700 --> 00:16:19.200
It's the same as before.

00:16:19.200 --> 00:16:23.610
While you think they haven't surrounded you, they've already limited your movements.

00:16:26.960 --> 00:16:28.720
I'm blocked at every turn.

00:16:29.580 --> 00:16:30.210
Here?

00:16:31.460 --> 00:16:32.590
I can't get out!

00:16:35.260 --> 00:16:37.180
Am I able to get out?

00:16:37.180 --> 00:16:38.850
It'll work!

00:16:38.850 --> 00:16:39.470
What the?!

00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:41.680
It's no use?

00:16:43.180 --> 00:16:46.770
Thanks to our previous battle,
I already understand how your mechas move.

00:16:46.770 --> 00:16:48.940
You won't get away this time!

00:16:48.940 --> 00:16:51.780
Damn it! There's no other way out, Dio!

00:16:52.090 --> 00:16:54.360
No. There's one more thing we haven't tried.

00:16:54.360 --> 00:16:55.740
You mean...?

00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:58.120
It will be even harder than before.

00:16:58.120 --> 00:17:01.330
Same to you. Don't start dragging me down.

00:17:05.210 --> 00:17:08.210
If both mechas are moving in sync,
then they'll be easier to capture.

00:17:08.210 --> 00:17:09.210
Surround them!

00:17:09.210 --> 00:17:09.960
Roger!

00:17:10.630 --> 00:17:12.380
The Valiancers are speeding up!

00:17:12.380 --> 00:17:15.130
Both mechas' Emphater levels are increasing.

00:17:15.130 --> 00:17:18.510
Don't tell me you're going to do a Code T2 Rise?!

00:17:18.510 --> 00:17:19.970
We sure are!

00:17:19.970 --> 00:17:20.810
Let's do it!

00:17:27.350 --> 00:17:28.650
What's that?

00:17:28.650 --> 00:17:30.770
The same technique was reported once from Chitose Base.

00:17:30.770 --> 00:17:33.070
Maintain formation. I'll take them down.

00:17:37.030 --> 00:17:38.780
It's our turn to attack!

00:17:38.780 --> 00:17:39.660
Yeah!

00:17:46.250 --> 00:17:47.080
Incredible!

00:17:47.080 --> 00:17:49.750
To maintain that position while attacking...

00:17:49.750 --> 00:17:53.420
Dio's waveform deviated after Coupling with Aoba-kun.

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:56.880
However, his potential is increasing instead.

00:17:56.880 --> 00:17:57.880
That means...

00:17:57.880 --> 00:18:02.600
A double-edged sword in battle may become an even stronger weapon.

00:18:03.350 --> 00:18:08.100
The effects of their Coupling are exceeding my expectations.

00:18:14.690 --> 00:18:16.950
W-Why are they able to do this?!

00:18:18.500 --> 00:18:20.070
You're finished!

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:28.330
This can't be.

00:18:28.620 --> 00:18:31.210
This plan was supposed to be perfect.

00:18:34.850 --> 00:18:36.170
Lord Dolzief!

00:18:41.680 --> 00:18:43.180
Time to counterattack!

00:18:43.180 --> 00:18:44.680
D-Don't falter!

00:18:45.800 --> 00:18:46.660
Retreat!

00:18:47.020 --> 00:18:49.440
Hey! Don't fall back whenever you please!

00:18:53.470 --> 00:18:54.690
Decoupling.

00:18:58.260 --> 00:19:00.530
Dio, let's go support the others.

00:19:03.200 --> 00:19:05.490
Coupling cancellation confirmed.

00:19:05.490 --> 00:19:07.250
Valiancer units launch.

00:19:07.250 --> 00:19:08.330
Roger!

00:19:08.330 --> 00:19:10.830
Full speed ahead towards the storm.

00:19:10.830 --> 00:19:12.420
Support the Imperial Army.

00:19:12.420 --> 00:19:13.590
Understood!

00:19:14.050 --> 00:19:16.420
According to our army's research,

00:19:16.420 --> 00:19:19.800
it takes time to recover once they have decoupled.

00:19:20.380 --> 00:19:25.260
It'd be problematic if we were accused of standing
idly by while the Imperial Army was crushed.

00:19:25.260 --> 00:19:26.970
Fall back immediately!

00:19:31.710 --> 00:19:32.310
Damn!

00:19:32.690 --> 00:19:33.810
They're making their move now?!

00:19:36.690 --> 00:19:38.280
Don't get caught in the storm!

00:19:38.280 --> 00:19:40.490
The National's new-type has started to move.

00:19:40.900 --> 00:19:42.410
Assume a battle formation!

00:19:42.410 --> 00:19:43.110
No.

00:19:43.110 --> 00:19:45.240
We're in no condition to fight.

00:19:45.950 --> 00:19:47.450
Escape into the storm.

00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:48.660
Into the storm?!

00:19:50.120 --> 00:19:51.040
Understood.

00:19:51.040 --> 00:19:53.460
Valiancer units, retreat immediately!

00:19:56.750 --> 00:19:58.630
I could've done a little more.

00:19:58.980 --> 00:20:00.630
You'll get caught if you keep complaining, y'know.

00:20:00.630 --> 00:20:03.010
Hurry up! You have a two-minute window to return!

00:20:03.010 --> 00:20:04.050
Roger!

00:20:04.050 --> 00:20:05.260
Dio and Aoba too, hurry up!

00:20:05.260 --> 00:20:06.140
Roger.

00:20:06.140 --> 00:20:07.560
Dio, enemies!

00:20:09.310 --> 00:20:10.350
This time...

00:20:10.350 --> 00:20:11.640
That's Hina's...

00:20:11.640 --> 00:20:12.770
At a time like this…

00:20:22.120 --> 00:20:23.740
Planning to flee into the storm, huh?

00:20:23.740 --> 00:20:27.660
It seems that the remaining forces of the Imperial Army have retreated.

00:20:27.660 --> 00:20:29.450
Should we turn back to attack them?

00:20:29.770 --> 00:20:33.460
We could shoot them down if we attack them head on.

00:20:33.460 --> 00:20:37.000
However, we came here to execute the next operation.

00:20:37.000 --> 00:20:39.090
We should avoid meaningless sacrifices.

00:20:39.320 --> 00:20:40.920
Roger.

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:42.340
Straight ahead!

00:20:42.340 --> 00:20:44.720
Valiancer units, break off pursuit.

00:20:44.720 --> 00:20:45.590
Roger!

00:20:45.590 --> 00:20:48.300
If we continue, we'll enter the eye of the storm.

00:20:48.300 --> 00:20:49.100
Turn back now!

00:20:49.100 --> 00:20:50.130
Roger!

00:20:52.730 --> 00:20:54.730
Bizon! Hina is still...

00:20:54.730 --> 00:20:56.480
What are you doing, Hina?!

00:20:56.480 --> 00:20:59.480
I'll obey orders once I defeat the enemy!

00:20:59.480 --> 00:21:01.650
Dammit. We're turning back.

00:21:01.650 --> 00:21:03.280
Hina, we're going back.

00:21:03.280 --> 00:21:05.200
That's what I usually do!

00:21:08.370 --> 00:21:10.450
Three Beryls have returned safely.

00:21:10.810 --> 00:21:12.450
Luxon and Bradyon?

00:21:12.450 --> 00:21:13.580
Returning soon.

00:21:15.080 --> 00:21:16.370
Bradyon, landing.

00:21:19.170 --> 00:21:20.630
Luxon, landing.

00:21:23.510 --> 00:21:25.010
Enemy of Zogilia!

00:21:25.340 --> 00:21:26.990
Hina, please stop!

00:21:28.720 --> 00:21:30.810
What are you doing? Fight back!

00:21:30.810 --> 00:21:32.270
But it's Hina!

00:21:32.530 --> 00:21:34.020
If only...

00:21:34.020 --> 00:21:35.770
If only you hadn't showed up!

00:21:36.130 --> 00:21:37.730
Hina, retreat now!

00:21:39.150 --> 00:21:40.020
Damn.

00:21:41.990 --> 00:21:42.650
Hina!

00:21:46.110 --> 00:21:47.700
I'm closing the hatch.

00:21:47.700 --> 00:21:48.820
It's too dangerous.

00:21:48.820 --> 00:21:50.330
Is the retrieval done?

00:21:50.610 --> 00:21:51.450
Luxon is...

00:21:53.200 --> 00:21:54.620
Stop this, Hina!

00:21:54.620 --> 00:21:55.410
Let go!

00:22:02.920 --> 00:22:03.630
Hurry up, Aoba!

00:22:06.880 --> 00:22:08.130
Watch out!

00:22:12.640 --> 00:22:14.600
Aoba!

00:22:17.090 --> 00:22:20.840
With my heart, I call out

00:22:20.840 --> 00:22:25.220
To the far side, mutually drawn

00:22:25.220 --> 00:22:29.730
Forgetting even the reason I ache

00:22:29.730 --> 00:22:34.360
Just for now, please

00:22:34.360 --> 00:22:38.530
I know you

00:22:38.530 --> 00:22:43.030
I'm searching for you

00:22:43.160 --> 00:22:45.490
Softly pressing my lips

00:22:45.490 --> 00:22:52.120
to the bright afterimage I can't keep from leaving

00:22:52.120 --> 00:23:00.670
If hesitation is what gives way to the slightest of hopes

00:23:00.670 --> 00:23:05.260
To the many gentle mornings...

00:23:05.260 --> 00:23:09.810
and the times I have wondered

00:23:09.810 --> 00:23:14.060
In the future that leads back to that sky,

00:23:14.060 --> 00:23:16.310
I want to save you,

00:23:16.310 --> 00:23:18.400
I want to protect you

00:23:18.400 --> 00:23:22.780
In the future that arrives at that dream

00:23:22.780 --> 00:23:25.660
Wait for me

00:23:25.660 --> 00:23:30.410
The love we'll surely find

00:23:30.410 --> 00:23:35.210
I want you to reach out for it

00:23:38.100 --> 00:23:40.630
Next episode, on Buddy Complex:

00:23:40.630 --> 00:23:42.050
"The Night of the Storm."
